**Subject.** When a member-requested meter test on an Electric Service by Rate Schedule account finds the meter fast beyond the schedule's accuracy tolerance, the test is settled by a meter error refund credit on the same service account. The credit names the meter test it settles and appears on the account at once and on the next bill.

**Observable effect.** Posting the credit adds one bill credit, dated today, naming the meter test record and the reason for the credit, and lowers the account's current balance by the amount credited.

## Posting the credit

**Situation of use and capability.** `post_meter_error_credit_d380ee62` posts a single bill credit on one electric service account, dated today, that names the meter test record it settles and the reason recorded for the credit, and lowers the account balance by the credited amount.

**How it is invoked.** It is an agent-side tool: unlock `post_meter_error_credit_d380ee62` with `unlock_agent_discoverable_tool`, then call it through `call_agent_discoverable_tool`.

**Parameters.**

- `service_account_id` — the reference number of the electric service account (one metered location) being credited, as shown by the service account lookup.
- `source_reference_id` — the reference number of the meter test record the credit settles, as shown by the trouble report and meter test lookup for the same account.
- `credit_reason` — why the credit is given; one of:
  - `deposit_refund` — a security deposit returned to the bill;
  - `deposit_application` — a held deposit applied against the balance;
  - `deposit_interest` — interest earned on a deposit paid out to the bill;
  - `capital_credit_retirement` — retired capital credits paid as a bill credit;
  - `capital_credit_offset` — capital credits offset against an unpaid balance;
  - `arrears_to_prepay` — a past-due amount moved onto a PrePay Power enrollment;
  - `prepay_balance_transfer` — a remaining prepaid balance moved back to the bill;
  - `arrears_to_arrangement` — a past-due amount moved into a payment arrangement;
  - `late_charge_waiver` — a courtesy waiver of one late payment charge;
  - `meter_error_refund` — money returned because a tested meter was found registering fast;
  - `billing_error_correction` — a line billed at the wrong schedule or quantity corrected;
  - `area_light_outage_credit` — credit for an area light that stayed out.
- `refund_amount` — the credit in USD, a positive amount with 2 decimal places, already rounded to the cent.

**Return.** On success the receipt carries `charge_id` (the reference number of the new bill credit), `service_account_id`, `source_reference_id` (the meter test the credit settles), `credit_reason` (the reason recorded), `amount` (USD with 2 decimal places), `charge_date` (YYYY-MM-DD, today), `account_balance` (the new balance, USD with 2 decimal places) and `status`, which reads "credited" when the credit is on the account.

### Contract questions

**Does the tool compute the refund?** No. It books the amount passed, already rounded to the cent.

**What does `source_reference_id` point at?** The meter test record of the same service account, as listed by the trouble report and meter test lookup.
